ke two components: ChatRow (no image) and ChatRowImage, or one component where instance can hide image (instance layer visibility override — allowed). One component \"ChatRow\" with image child; toggle visible per instance. Question text override per instance.\n\n**Cmp/ExportRow**: horizontal: PDF icon (44) + column(title bold 14, date caption) + size (caption) maybe right. Padding, border bottom or card. I'll do card rows: radius 16 border white fill.\n\n**Cmp/SuggestionCard**: vertical, border, radius 16, padding 14: title (Nunito Bold 14) + detail (13 secondary, 2 lines). Grid 2×2.\n\n**Cmp/InputBar**: horizontal: text field \"Ask me anything...\" fill width + send button (48 circle primary with Icon_Send white). \n\n**Cmp/HeaderChat**: row: Icon_Menu (left), center: logo 32 + col(\"Chat Bot AI 4.5\" bold 15, \"Premium account\" caption primary?), right: Icon_Export. \n\n**Cmp/BubbleYou**: right-aligned column: label \"You\" caption right; bubble primary fill, white text 15, radius 20 (corner 4 bottom-right); actions row (chips: Icon_Edit+Edit, Icon_Copy+Copy).\n**Cmp/BubbleAI**: left-aligned column: label \"Chat Bot AI\" with small logo 20; bubble #F4F1F6 fill, text 15 dark, radius 20 (4 bottom-left); actions row chips (Copy/Share/Regenerate or Download/Share/Regenerate); optional image child (for image message).\nAction chip: small pill with icon 14 + label 12 semibold, border or ghost. \n\n**Cmp/SettingsRow**: horizontal: icon? Settings list: Email (with value sam.rivera@example.com), Change password (chevron), Theme (value \"System default\" + chevron), Data & storage (value \"83% Used\" + chevron), Send feedback (chevron) + below note text. Row: label left bold-ish 15, right value caption + Icon_Arrow_Up_Right? chevron — no chevron icon given; use Icon_Arrow_Up_Right (given) as the \"go\" affordance. Good.\n\n**Cmp/FooterLegal**: column centered: \"Chat Bot AI - Version 2.0.5\" caption, row \"Terms of use\" · \"Privacy policy\" links primary.\n\n**Cmp/Sheet**: container: fill white, top radius 28, padding, drag handle bar. Content varies — build per-screen contents but reuse sheet shell component with children? Instances can't add children. So sheet shell as component with fixed children won't flex. Instead I'll build sheets inline per screen (still styled consistently). For \"component reuse\" credit, the shell could be a component used 3 times but content differs... I'll make SheetShell component with handle + title slot only, and accept that content is added per instance? Can't add to instance. Alternative: make each sheet a component itself (Sheet_Export, Sheet_Account, Sheet_Theme) — each used once but they're components. Fine.\n\nActually simpler: sheets built inline in frames 07/09/10 with consistent styling. Componentization credit comes from the many other components. OK.\n\n**Cmp/ThemeRow**: row: radio circle + label; selected: filled primary radio. Component with variant selected true/false → two variants or one comp with toggling via instance override (set fills). I'll make component \"ThemeRow\" and per instance override radio fill + label weight.\n\nStorage bar: stacked horizontal bar with 3 segments + remaining, rounded. Build inline (one use).\n\nOK, also \"tap outside → 08\" links: add reaction on the dim overlay region behind sheet.\n\nGiven the complexity, let me start executing. Call 1: setup page, load fonts, clone kit components, create kit frame, return ID registry.\n\nOne concern: page 5:2 may already contain something. Check and report. Let me write call 1.\n\nNote: text nodes I create require loaded fonts. In call 1 I create kit labels? Skip text in call 1 except maybe none.\n\nLet me also decide screen heights now:\n- 01: 928\n- 02: compute: statusbar 47; header rows: topbar 48, brand row ~56 (logo 40 + text), NewTopic 48, History section: label 22 + search 48 → ~80 with spacing, viewswitch 46. Header total ≈ 47+16+48+12+56+16+48+20+80+16+46+16 = 471? Hmm let me not compute precisely; use auto-layout with fixed frame height set after content: I'll create frame with primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO (hug) so height fits content! Frame 428 wide, hug height. Then frame heights auto-computed. But top-level frames with hug are fine. I'll set frame.layoutMode VERTICAL, primaryAxisSizingMode 'AUTO', counter fixed 428, clipsContent true. Then exact heights emerge naturally. \n\nFor 928-fixed frames, set fixed height 928 and use space-between or absolute bottom elements.\n\nScreen grid: I'll position frames manually after creation, reading their heights.\n\nPrototype: after building, set reactions on trigger nodes (instances/layers) with `node.reactions = [{action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE'...} or null}, trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}]`. For \"tap outside\" use the overlay rect.\n\nTransition: simple dissolve/instant. Use transition {type:'DISSOLVE', duration:0.2, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}} or SMART_ANIMATE for sheets (MOVE_IN from bottom would be nice but destination is full frame; use SMART_ANIMATE). Keep simple: SMART_ANIMATE 300ms for all? SMART_ANIMATE between full frames fine.\n\nLet me write Call 1 now. Keep code under 50k chars. I'll return registry mapping name→id.\n\nAlso important: preserve reference pages — cloning doesn't modify originals. Good.\n\nKit frame: figma.createFrame, name \"00 · Kit · Components & Assets\", layout vertical wrap? Just place clones in a grid manually: simple approach — put all clones in a vertical AL frame with itemSpacing 16 and let it hug; visual tidiness not critical for kit. But components at various sizes fine.\n\nAlso: component clones moved to another page: `clone()` then `kitFrame.appendChild(c)`. If c is a component on another page, appendChild reparents it. OK.\n\nLet me also handle: the workspace page might have existing content — check children, if empty proceed; if has content, place kit after it.\n\nCall 1 code:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\n// font load test\nasync function tryLoad(family, style){ try { await figma.loadFontAsync({family, style}); return true; } catch(e){ return false; } }\nconst fontReport = {};\nfor (const s of ['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','SemiBold','Bold','Extra Bold','ExtraBold']) fontReport['Bricolage Grotesque '+s] = await tryLoad('Bricolage Grotesque', s);\nfor (const s of ['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold','ExtraBold']) fontReport['Nunito '+s] = await tryLoad('Nunito', s);\nconst ids = ['3:24','3:29','3:34','3:45','4:8','4:11','4:19','4:22','4:25','4:28','4:31','4:42','4:48','4:58','4:64','4:70','4:76','4:82','4:87','4:94','4:101','4:110','4:116','4:121','4:128','4:134','4:139','4:145','4:152','4:157','4:164','4:171','4:177','4:182','4:189','4:197'];\nconst kit = figma.createFrame();\nkit.name = 'Kit · Components & Assets';\nkit.x = 0; kit.y = 0;\nkit.layoutMode = 'VERTICAL'; kit.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; kit.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\nkit.itemSpacing = 24; kit.paddingLeft=kit.paddingRight=kit.paddingTop=kit.paddingBottom=48;\nkit.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color:{r:0.98,g:0.98,b:0.985}}];\nconst registry = {};\nfor (const id of ids) {\n  const n = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  if (n) { const c = n.clone(); kit.appendChild(c); registry[c.name] = c.id; }\n}\nconst existing = page.children.map(c=>({id:c.id,name:c.name,type:c.type}));\nreturn { fontReport, registry, existingBefore: existing };\n```\n\nWait — kit frame created while currentPage is workspace page → appended to current page automatically. Good.\n\nThen Call 2: create new components. I'll write helpers and create: ViewSwitch (variant set), HeaderHome, SearchField, BtnNewTopic, ChatRow, ExportRow, SuggestionCard, InputBar, HeaderChat, BubbleYou, BubbleAI, ActionChip(s), SettingsRow, FooterLegal, ThemeRow, SectionHeader, PdfIconBadge etc.\n\nTo limit risk, I'll build components in 2 calls (2a, 2b), checking results.\n\nHelper functions needed (redefined each call):\n```js\nconst C = { primary:{r:0.3804,g:0.1647,b:0.4549}, primaryDark:{r:0.29,g:0.12,b:0.35}, soft:{r:0.957,g:0.929,b:0.969}, surface:{r:0.976,g:0.969,b:0.980}, white:{r:1,g:1,b:1}, text:{r:0.118,g:0.102,b:0.133}, sub:{r:0.435,g:0.408,b:0.459}, faint:{r:0.604,g:0.576,b:0.620}, border:{r:0.906,g:0.886,b:0.918}, error:{r:0.851,g:0.176,b:0.125}, errorSoft:{r:0.996,g:0.953,b:0.949}, warn:{r:0.71,g:0.278,b:0.031}, warnSoft:{r:1,g:0.98,b:0.922}, chat:{r:0.3804,g:0.1647,b:0.4549}, img:{r:0.659,g:0.42,b:0.769}, exp:{r:0.851,g:0.722,b:0.910}, free:{r:0.937,g:0.918,b:0.949} };\n```\nRGB: primary #612A74 → 0.3804, 0.1647, 0.4549 ✓.\n\nFont style resolution: after trying loads, pick: bricBold = 'Bold' loaded? else fallback; store in global consts BRIC_BOLD etc. Each call re-derives.\n\nText helper:\n```js\nfunction txt(str, family, style, size, color, opts={}) {\n  const t = figma.createText();\n  t.fontName = {family, style};\n  t.characters = str;\n  t.fontSize = size;\n  t.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color}];\n  if (opts.lh) t.lineHeight = {unit:'PIXELS', value: opts.lh};\n  if (opts.ls !== undefined) t.letterSpacing = {unit:'PIXELS', value: opts.ls};\n  if (opts.align) t.textAlignHorizontal = opts.align;\n  if (opts.w === 'fill') { t.layoutAlign = 'STRETCH'; t.textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'; }\n  else if (opts.w) { t.textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'; t.resize(opts.w, t.height); }\n  return t;\n}\n```\nCareful: setting textAutoResize HEIGHT with layoutAlign STRETCH inside AL parent works.\n\nAL helper:\n```js\nfunction al(node, dir, opts={}) {\n  node.layoutMode = dir;\n  node.itemSpacing = opts.gap ?? 0;\n  node.paddingLeft=opts.pl??opts.p??0; ... etc\n  node.primaryAxisAlignItems = opts.main ?? 'MIN';\n  node.counterAxisAlignItems = opts.cross ?? 'MIN';\n  node.primaryAxisSizingMode = opts.mainSize ?? 'AUTO';\n  node.counterAxisSizingMode = opts.crossSize ?? 'AUTO';\n}\n```\n\nIcon instance helper:\n```js\nasync function icon(name, size, color) {\n  const comp = await findComp(