: SettingsRow component (label, value, arrow) and the feedback note as separate element under the row inside the card.\n\nFooter: spacer; FooterLegal component: \"Chat Bot AI - Version 2.0.5\" caption faint; row: \"Terms of use\" \"Privacy policy\" Nunito SemiBold 13 primary with dot separator. HomeIndicator.\n\nSPACE_BETWEEN: top group / bottom footer.\n\n### 09_Account_Actions_Sheet (928)\nBehind: 08 replica dimmed. To replicate cheaply: same components again (topbar, profile block, settings card) — reuse components, fine. Overlay black 0.4. Sheet bottom: handle; rows: \"Sign out\" (with Icon? use Icon_Arrow_Up_Right? better Icon_Back rotated? Just text rows with icons: Sign out → Icon_Export? Hmm. Use text-only rows: two full-width list buttons h 52: \"Sign out\" (text dark, centered? left). Design: card rows radius 16 border: Sign out (label center, bold 16, dark); Delete Account (label center bold 16 error red, errorSoft fill?). I'll do: sheet padding 24 gap 12: two buttons: Btn ghost \"Sign out\" (surface fill), Btn danger soft \"Delete Account\". Add close? Spec only lists the two actions. Tap outside → 08.\n\n### 10_Theme_Sheet (928)\n08 replica dimmed + sheet: handle, title \"Theme\" (Bricolage Bold 18), 3 ThemeRow options: Light mode, Dark mode, System default (selected radio). Radio: circle 22 border 2; selected: primary border + inner dot. Tap outside → 08. Also tapping other rows could go nowhere (entry only).\n\n### 11_Cloud_Space (hug)\nRoot: StatusBar; topbar: back + \"Cloud Space\" title + more.\nContent column padding 24 gap 20:\n- Usage card: \"12.48 GB of 15 GB used\" Bricolage Bold 20; stacked bar h 12 radius full: segments: chats 25% #612A74, images 55% #A86BC4, exports 3% #D9B8E8, rest free #EFEAF2. Legend rows: dot + \"Chats\" + \"25%\" right; Images 55%; Exports 3%.\n- Images card: row: \"Images\" Bricolage Bold 17 + \"169 Item\" caption; \"8,225 MB\" bold right? Layout: title row: Images + count chip; size right. Note text caption sub (the cache note). Thumbnails row: 7 thumbs ~48×48 radius 10, scroll row (Mug, Rat, Statue, Student, Mug, Rat, Statue).\n- Exports card: \"Exports\" + \"37 Item\", \"506 MB\"; note caption; 3 mini rows: PDF icon 36 + col(title 13 bold, date caption) + size caption + delete iconbtn (Icon_Delete error).\n- Danger zone card: \"Clear cache\" row + \"238.05 MB\" + arrow → 12; divider; \"Delete all chats\" + \"12.48 GB\"; warning box: errorSoft bg, Icon? text: \"Warning! By deleting all chats, all photos, conversations and documents will be lost and cannot be recovered!\" caption error color.\n- FooterLegal; HomeIndicator.\n\n### 12_Clear_Cache_Dialog (928)\n11 replica (top portion: topbar + usage card + start of images card) dimmed + centered dialog: white radius 24 padding 24: \"Clear cache\" Bricolage Bold 20 center; text 14 sub center: \"You are requesting to delete a cache with a size of 238.05 MB. Are you sure about your request?\"; row: Cancel (ghost, fill width) + Delete (error fill, white text, fill width). Cancel → 11, Delete → 11.\n\nReactions summary (prototype):\n- 01: Button(Login) → 02\n- 02: BtnNewTopic → 05; ChatRow#2 → 06; ViewSwitch: Images tab → 03, Exports tab → 04; Avatar → 08\n- 03: ViewSwitch Chats → 02, Exports → 04; NewTopic → 05 (HeaderHome instance's inner button — reactions on nested instance layers allowed)\n- 04: ViewSwitch Chats → 02, Images → 03; NewTopic → 05\n- 05: menu iconbtn → 02\n- 06: menu → 02; export iconbtn → 07\n- 07: close → 06; Export btn → 06; overlay → 06\n- 08: back → 02; more → 09; Theme row → 10; Data & storage row → 11\n- 09: Sign out → 01; overlay → 08\n- 10: overlay → 08\n- 11: back → 08; Clear cache row → 12\n- 12: Cancel → 11; Delete → 11\n\nNote: nested-layer reactions on instances are supported (reactions on instance children). I'll verify after setting.\n\nExecution plan (calls):\n1. Setup + clone kit + fonts report. ✓\n2. Create base new components: Field, IconBtn? (inline helper not component), BtnNewTopic, SearchField, ViewSwitch set (3 variants), ChatRow, ExportRow, SuggestionCard, ActionChip, InputBar, HeaderHome, HeaderChat, BubbleYou, BubbleAI, SettingsRow, FooterLegal, ThemeRow. This is a LOT for one call; split:\n   2a: helpers + Field, BtnNewTopic, SearchField, ActionChip, SuggestionCard, ExportRow, ChatRow.\n   2b: ViewSwitch variants, HeaderHome, HeaderChat, BubbleYou, BubbleAI, SettingsRow, FooterLegal, ThemeRow, InputBar.\n3. Screens 01 + 05.\n4. Screens 02 + 03 + 04.\n5. Screen 06.\n6. Screens 07.\n7. Screen 08 + 09 + 10.\n8. Screen 11 + 12.\n9. Reactions wiring.\n10. Screenshots all 12, fix issues.\n\nAlso place screen frames: row layout x step 480, y groups. I'll position as I go: track x cursor per row. Row A (01,02,03,04) at y=kit bottom + 200. Actually simpler: screens start at fixed coordinates: I'll compute after kit done. Let me place screens starting y=1400 (kit ~ maybe 1600 tall?). Kit has 39 items vertical × ~100 avg = huge (~4000px). Hmm kit vertical AL hug — fine, screens start below kit: I'll read kit height and set yScreens = kit.y + kit.height + 240. Do this per call by querying kit node.\n\nActually components CAN live on the workspace page directly (top-level) without containing frame; but a kit frame keeps tidy. Vertical list 4000px is ugly but fine. Better: kit as WRAP layout with fixed width 1200: layoutMode HORIZONTAL + layoutWrap WRAP, itemSpacing 24, counterAxisSpacing 24, width fixed 1240, hug height. → height ~ (39 items avg 100 wide → ~8 rows × 130 = 1040). \n\nLet me write Call 1.\n\nAlso note: getNodeByIdAsync for ids across pages works regardless of current page. setCurrentPageAsync needed before creating (createFrame adds to currentPage).\n\nOne more check: Workspace page 5:2 exists and may be empty. I'll list children.\n\nAlso there's a subtlety: \"clone()\" of a component from another page — clone places it as sibling (same parent page). Then appendChild to kit (on workspace page) moves it. Should be allowed.\n\nLet me write call 1 now. Keep return small.\n\nAfter that, I'll do component calls. Given code length constraints, I'll be economical: define helpers compactly.\n\nLet me also extract image hashes in call 1 to use later — but simpler to re-derive in each call: `const imgHash = async name => (await findComp(name)).fills[0].imageHash;`\n\nNow — write Call 1.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0338c781-78cf-48da-b153-97e8b743ce85","uuid":"7fdabeb9-7713-4a88-a9d7-8a8a51834c83","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:48:27.471Z","thinking_duration_ms":397988}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":34609,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02106ae57f8b0a7a5bfe284c612630ad","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need: brand color #612A74, fonts Bricolage Grotesque + Nunito, given components' exact specs, all media assets, and the full story text. Now I'll set up the workspace: switch to page 03 · Workspace, load fonts, and clone all given components and media assets into a kit frame there."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0338c781-78cf-48da-b153-97e8b743ce85","uuid":"838223b8-8eef-4b32-acd5-0d392503286b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:48:29.667Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":34609,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02106ae57f8b0a7a5bfe284c612630ad","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_8_42832f83","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"lEwCWXljcAXgGd3yvwjAbG","code":"const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst existing = page.children.map(c=>({id:c.id,name:c.name,type:c.type,w:c.width,h:c.height}));\n\nasync function tryLoad(family, style){ try { await figma.loadFontAsync({family, style}); return true; } catch(e){ return false; } }\nconst fontReport = {};\nfor (const s of ['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','SemiBold','Bold','Extra Bold','ExtraBold']) fontReport['Bricolage|'+s] = await tryLoad('Bricolage Grotesque', s);\nfor (const s of ['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold','ExtraBold']) fontReport['Nunito|'+s] = await tryLoad('Nunito', s);\n\nconst ids = ['3:24','3:29','3:34','3:45','4:8','4:11','4:19','4:22','4:25','4:28','4:31','4:42','4:48','4:58','4:64','4:70','4:76','4:82','4:87','4:94','4:101','4:110','4:116','4:121','4:128','4:134','4:139','4:145','4:152','4:157','4:164','4:171','4:177','4:182','4:189','4:197'];\nconst kit = figma.createFrame();\nkit.name = 'Kit · Components & Assets';\nkit.x = 0; kit.y = 0;\nkit.layoutMode = 'HORIZONTAL';\nkit.layoutWrap = 'WRAP';\nkit.itemSpacing = 24; kit.counterAxisSpacing = 24;\nkit.paddingLeft=kit.paddingRight=kit.paddingTop=kit.paddingBottom=48;\nkit.counterAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO';\nkit.resize(1240, kit.height);\nkit.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color:{r:0.985,g:0.98,b:0.99}}];\nconst registry = {};\nfor (const id of ids) {\n  const n = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  if (n) { const c = n.clone(); kit.appendChild(c); registry[c.name] = c.id; }\n}\nreturn { fontReport, registry, kitId: kit.id, existingBefore: existing };","description":"Set up workspace page, load fonts, clone given components/media into a kit frame"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0338c781-78cf-48da-b153-97e8b743ce85","uuid":"1e0ed88e-78a4-46d4-97a6-cea8ceb50638","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:48:37.257Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_8_42832f83","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
